Vaginal examination at that time showed the cervix was 8cm dilated but was
otherwise unchanged from one hour previously. Which one of the following would be
he most appropriate next step in management?','{"A":"Immediate delivery by Caesarean section.","B":"Further fetal scalp pH assessment.","C":". Allow labour to proceed with continuous CTG evaluation.\nAugment labour with Syntocinon®/oxytocin.","D":"Perform a ventouse delivery.","E":"MOQ2>"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[361],"source_qid":"3.315","duplicate_group_id":"exact-2e31aefdab52","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"b2638dde96f4750ea751","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":361,"source_qid":"3.315"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"b2638dde96f4750ea751","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":361,"supporting_pages":[361],"source_qid":"3.315","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Ausiralian Medical Council\nSection 3 — Maternal Health\nMCQ 3.315\nA 23-year-old woman is found to have a temperature of 37.9°C three days after a\nlower uterine segment Caesarean section delivery (LUSCS) for obstructed labour at\nterm. She had been given one dose of prophylactic antibiotics intraoperatively. Prior\nto today she had been afebrile during the post-partum period. Which one of the\nfollowing is least likely to be the cause of her fever?\nAn abdominal wound infection.\nBreast engorgement.\n. Acute endometritis.\nA deep venous thrombosis (DVT).\nA urinary tract infection.\nTMOOP>\nMCQ 3.316\nA 25-year-old woman, in her first pregnancy, has been in spontaneous labour at term\nfor 6 hours. The membranes ruptured two hours ago and the liquor was meconium\nstained. Cardiotocography (CTG) was therefore commenced and showed some\nintermittent late decelerations, from 140 down to 110/min. Vaginal examination\nshowed the cervix was 5cm dilated, the presentation was cephalic, position left\noccipitotransverse (LOT), and the bony head was at the level of the ischial spines (IS).\nBecause of the deceleration pattern a fetal scalp pH estimation was performed and\nthe pH was shown to be 7.32. One hour later the CTG showed the following pattern\nover the preceding period of 30 minutes.\nBaseline 40/min\nBaseline variability /min\nAccelerations None evident\nDecelerations Two decelerations were evident, with the heart rate\n‘alling to 80/min, and with each lasting 4 minutes\nVaginal examination at that time showed the cervix was 8cm dilated but was\notherwise unchanged from one hour previously. Which one of the following would be\nhe most appropriate next step in management?","options":{"A":"Immediate delivery by Caesarean section.","B":"Further fetal scalp pH assessment.","C":". Allow labour to proceed with continuous CTG evaluation.\nAugment labour with Syntocinon®/oxytocin.","D":"Perform a ventouse delivery.","E":"MOQ2>"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","antibiotic","dose","management","pregnan","prophyl"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"medium","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"2e31aefdab52da9550d5c9a375ab0e78b96bef47","duplicate_group_id":"exact-2e31aefdab52","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"b2638dde96f4750ea751","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multipl