likely to result in a pregnancy loss, but still enabling the diagnosis to be made) to
: definitely exclude the presence of Trisomy 21 in the fetus in this pregnancy?','{"A":"Nuchal translucency at 11-12 weeks of gestation.","B":"Chorion villus biopsy (CVB) at 10-12 weeks of gestation. /","C":"Amniocentesis at 16 weeks of gestation. ;","D":"Maternal serum screening for alpha-fetoprotein, beta-hCG and oestradiol levels.","E":"Cordocentesis at 18 weeks of gestation.\n_speseeeneae tenes ennenonnanneesesoesasuassessssssseeassssssessssisasasdsteassosssssessusssssssstesasttssreeseossssasussanneaseerssnssesssassuseennsseosssaseneees |\nMCQ 3.325\n''"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[364],"source_qid":"3.323","duplicate_group_id":"exact-2407d4a1913c","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"52ffded782e05d82df17","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":364,"source_qid":"3.323"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_multi_group","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"52ffded782e05d82df17","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":364,"supporting_pages":[364],"source_qid":"3.323","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Ausiralian Medical Council\nf Section 3 — Maternal Health\n{ ee ee ee tar ee ira eee eT er a eee ee\nMCQ 3.323 |\ni]\ni You are managing the pregnancy of a 30-year-old woman who had. a fetus with\nH spina bifida in her only previous pregnancy. Which one of the following assessments is\nthe most appropriate to enable recognition of this condition should it recur in the current\npregnancy?\nA. Maternal alpha-fetoprotein at 11-12 weeks of gestation.\ni B. Maternal alpha-fetoprotein at 15-16 weeks of gestation.\nC. Ultrasound of the fetal spine at 16-18 weeks of gestation. |\nD. Ultrasound of the fetal head at 11-12 weeks of gestation. .\n; E. Ultrasound of the nuchal translucency at 11-12 weeks of gestation.\nMCQ 3.324\nA 39-year-old woman (gravida 2, para 1) attends for her first antenatal visit at eight\nweeks of gestation in her second pregnancy and is concerned about the risk of Down\n+] syndrome in the fetus. Which one of the following is the safest test (i.e. the one least\nlikely to result in a pregnancy loss, but still enabling the diagnosis to be made) to\n: definitely exclude the presence of Trisomy 21 in the fetus in this pregnancy?","options":{"A":"Nuchal translucency at 11-12 weeks of gestation.","B":"Chorion villus biopsy (CVB) at 10-12 weeks of gestation. /","C":"Amniocentesis at 16 weeks of gestation. ;","D":"Maternal serum screening for alpha-fetoprotein, beta-hCG and oestradiol levels.","E":"Cordocentesis at 18 weeks of gestation.\n_speseeeneae tenes ennenonnanneesesoesasuassessssssseeassssssessssisasasdsteassosssssessusssssssstesasttssreeseossssasussanneaseerssnssesssassuseennsseosssaseneees |\nMCQ 3.325\n''"},"options_mode":"text","source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["pregnan"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_multi_group","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"2407d4a1913c4199cbfd0d359ac429d03ecf774f","duplicate_group_id":"exact-2407d4a1913c","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"52ffded782e05d82df17","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple