Section 3 — Maternal Health
re 1 SSS 0 SSS CO I ISL
MCQ 3.326
A 32-year-old woman, who is at 20 weeks of gestation in her first pregnancy, has been
found to have herpes simplex type 2 virus on a swab taken from a vulval ulcer. She
has never had such a lesion before and her partner of 12 years has had no previous
history of infection. She is clearly concerned about how she contracted the disease
and any effects it may have on her or her unborn child. Which one of the following is
the most appropriate advice?','{"A":"Unless she has had a new sexual partner recently, this problem could not have\nbeen acquired sexually.","B":"The primary infection is commonly asymptomatic.","C":"Treatment with aciclovir will reduce the rate of recurrent disease but is\ncontraindicated in pregnancy because of adverse effects on the fetus.","D":"The risk of neonatal herpes is much higher if there is a recurrence of previous genital\nherpes near the time of delivery than if a primary infection occurs at the time.","E":"Most children with neonatal herpes present with mucocutaneous lesions."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.326","duplicate_group_id":"exact-d5e2ae90908a","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"919958f602502158bb59","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":365,"source_qid":"3.326"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"919958f602502158bb59","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":365,"source_qid":"3.326","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council\nSection 3 — Maternal Health\nre 1 SSS 0 SSS CO I ISL\nMCQ 3.326\nA 32-year-old woman, who is at 20 weeks of gestation in her first pregnancy, has been\nfound to have herpes simplex type 2 virus on a swab taken from a vulval ulcer. She\nhas never had such a lesion before and her partner of 12 years has had no previous\nhistory of infection. She is clearly concerned about how she contracted the disease\nand any effects it may have on her or her unborn child. Which one of the following is\nthe most appropriate advice?","options":{"A":"Unless she has had a new sexual partner recently, this problem could not have\nbeen acquired sexually.","B":"The primary infection is commonly asymptomatic.","C":"Treatment with aciclovir will reduce the rate of recurrent disease but is\ncontraindicated in pregnancy because of adverse effects on the fetus.","D":"The risk of neonatal herpes is much higher if there is a recurrence of previous genital\nherpes near the time of delivery than if a primary infection occurs at the time.","E":"Most children with neonatal herpes present with mucocutaneous lesions."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["pregnan"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"d5e2ae90908acfbd155c0da12e1fdb95a71edd58","duplicate_group_id":"exact-d5e2ae90908a","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"919958f602502158bb59","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":365,"source_qid":"3.326"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_