: MCQ 3.339
q In evaluating the characteristics of a screening test for a psychiatric disorder, it is
important to know of the prevalence of the disorder in the sample population. If the
prevalence is low, which one of the following statements about sensitivity, specificity,
positive and negative predictive power, and reliability is correct?','{"A":"Sensitivity will be lower.","B":"Specificity will be higher.","C":"Positive predictive power will be lower.","D":"Reliability will be higher.","E":"Negative predictive power will be unchanged.\n| MCQ 3.340"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[370],"source_qid":"3.338","duplicate_group_id":"exact-174ae5965b55","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"9c4dc16d2417825b9b18","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":370,"source_qid":"3.338"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_multi_group","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"9c4dc16d2417825b9b18","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":370,"supporting_pages":[370],"source_qid":"3.338","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council See tg :\nii is not the first time that she has fainted during a gym workout. As part of a mental state\nassessment of this woman, which one of the following is the most likely abnormality in\nher cognitive content?\ni A. Thoughts about suicide.\ni B. Fears of losing control.\ni C. Obsessions about cleanliness.\n1 D. Concerns about her weight and shape.\n1 E. Infatuation with a fellow student.\ni MCQ 3.338\n| A 48-year-old man has chronic low back pain as a result of lifting heavy boxes at\ni work four years previously. He is now not working and is on a pension having had a\ni disability insurance claim settled. A magnetic resonance scan has confirmed a low\nii lumbar disc prolapse without neurocompression. He complains that paracetamol\n| two tablets (each 500mg) on an ‘as needed’ basis up to four times a day is not suffi-\n| cient to alleviate his pain. Which one of the following is the most appropriate next\nit | step in his pain management?\n}\n+ A. Add amitriptyline 150mg daily.\ni B. Add buprenorphene (Norspan®) patches weekly.\n| C. Change to aspirin ‘as needed’.\nIH it D. Change to regular paracetamol.\nH | | E. Change to a regular nonsteroidal anti-infammatory analgesic.\n: MCQ 3.339\nq In evaluating the characteristics of a screening test for a psychiatric disorder, it is\nimportant to know of the prevalence of the disorder in the sample population. If the\nprevalence is low, which one of the following statements about sensitivity, specificity,\npositive and negative predictive power, and reliability is correct?","options":{"A":"Sensitivity will be lower.","B":"Specificity will be higher.","C":"Positive predictive power will be lower.","D":"Reliability will be higher.","E":"Negative predictive power will be unchanged.\n| MCQ 3.340"},"options_mode":"text","source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","management","screen","screening"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_multi_group","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"174ae5965b554e8682bfb208b64d064eb366c7de","duplicate_group_id":"exact-174ae5965b55","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"9c4dc16d2417825b9b18","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Ver