Section 3 - Mental Health
MCQ 3.348
Nonfatal deliberate self-inflicted injury is common in Australia. Which one of the
following is the most popular site of self-inflicted injury in Australia?
. Wrist.
Leg.
. Torso.
. Head and neck.
Genitalia.
MFO @) 3>
MCQ 3.349
Most psychotropic drugs are lipophilic. This means that:
A. they are better absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract when taken with meals
B. they are more resistant to hepatic metabolism
C. they bind readily to circulating free fatty acids
D.
E
. they pass easily from the bloodstream to the brain
. they are less likely to have active metabolites.
