MCQ 3.351
Which one of the following is the most striking feature when interviewing a patient
with thought disorder?','{"A":"You experience a ‘pressure’ in the patient''s talk and you have difficulty keeping\nup with the patient''s flow of ideas.\nB. The patient withdraws to the extent that you have difficulty maintaining contact.\nC. The patient is forgetful and has difficulty remembering what he/she is talking\nabout.\n- You cannot quite grasp the meaning of some of the patient''s statements.\nIt is as though a pane of glass is between you and the patient.","B":"mo","C":"3.352","D":"A 22-year-old real estate employee has been brought to the Emergency Department\nfor assessment by the police after suddenly assaulting two friends during a trivial\nargument at a local hotel. He had consumed only half a glass of beer — about 200mL.\nHe is quite calm, ashamed and very contrite. He says that he had previously become\nviolent and aggressive several times over the past four years, damaging property or\npunching and attacking strangers or former schoolmates with minimal provocation.\nPhysical examination and mental state are normal apart from minor injuries to his","E":"A RES"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[373],"source_qid":"3.348","duplicate_group_id":"exact-ab4d49c74dcf","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"0c39577ebf57063a1432","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":373,"source_qid":"3.348"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"0c39577ebf57063a1432","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (