te the patient''s treatment chart. Which one\nof the following is the most appropriate response to this request?\n\nRing up the night resident.\n\nContact your Medical Defence Association.\n\n. Refer the matter to the senior Emergency Department clinician.\nSign for the medication and complete the treatment chart.\nRing up the patient.\n\nMOQOR>\n\n|| mca3.358\n\n} A 70-year-old woman presents with a history of disturbed sleep, tearfulness, waves of\n| anxiety and chest pain for the past two weeks. Her husband had died suddenly about\nthis time a year ago of a heart attack, but in the last week she has been woken up\nby his voice calling out her name. She is alarmed and distressed by this and is worried\nshe may also be having angina or losing her mind. Her electrocardiogram (ECG)\nshows a mild sinus tachycardia only, but her troponin level is not raised and physical\nexamination is normal. Which one of the following is the most likely explanation for her\npresentation?\n\nof\n\n357"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"low","currentness_keywords":[],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"d2c8f299c66c9f4f83d147f45ea3dd5c3bcbb4a3","duplicate_group_id":"exact-d2c8f299c66c","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"bab18f6fcda6c8fc0fdb","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":375,"source_qid":"3.357"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_jso