sh most likely diagnosis?','{"A":"A. Asperger syndrome.","B":"Childhood disintegrative disorder.","C":"Deafness.","D":"Autism.","E":"Intellectual impairment.\nMCQ 3.363\nA 15-year-old school boy is brought by his mother to a general practice. His mother\nsays that the boy’s father has a schizophrenic illness and she is concerned about\n| recent changes in her son''s behaviour. He has become subdued and is spending a lot\nof his time lying on his bed listening to his iPod. She wonders if he may be developing\n| a psychosis like his father. In assessing this patient''s history which one of the following\n| is most likely to be associated with an evolving psychosis?\n__ FF 359"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.361","duplicate_group_id":"exact-a2fa56e1ded4","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"f3a52ff45276721dda43","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":377,"source_qid":"3.361"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"f3a52ff45276721dda43","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":377,"source_qid":"3.361","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council\n: : ities aa ___ Section 3- Mental Health |\nMCQ 3.361\nA 16-year-old girl self-presents requesting medication to help her sleep. When she tries\nto sleep she finds her thoughts repeatedly go over ‘all the stupid things | did today’.\n_4 | Getting off