A. Truancy.
/ B. A drop in grades at school.
C. Angry outbursts.
D. Arecent relationship break-up.
E. Loss of employment. :
MCQ 3.364
Relatives report a gradual decline in memory and self-care skills in a 75-year-old man
over several years. Examination reveals that he is disoriented in time, has poor short-
term memory, impaired planning, arithmetic and visuo spatial skills. There are no
. other abnormal findings. Which one of the following is the most appropriate initial step
in management?
A. Lumbar puncture.
B. Computed tomography (CT) of head.
C. Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) of the brain.
D. Cholinesterase inhibitor medication.
E. Serum electrolytes and creatinine.
MCQ 3.365
A previously well 40-year-old man presents to the Emergency Department complaining
| of tightness in the chest, palpitations, blurred vision, sweating and light-headedness,
all of which came on suddenly a few hours ago while serving on a jury. He feels
apprehensive and thinks that he has had a heart attack. He hopes that this is not so,
as he is planning to take a holiday after the court case has finished. On examination
he is somewhat agitated and has cold, clammy hands. His pulse rate is 80/min and
regular, respiratory rate is 13/min. The remainder of his physical examination is normal. ;
Electrocardiogram (ECG) and serum cardiac enzyme troponin levels are normal, and
you have concluded that no further physical investigation is required. Which one of
the following is the most likely cause of his symptoms?','{"A":"Caffeine intoxication.","B":"Malingering.","C":"Conversion disorder.","D":"Panic attack.","E":"Post-traumatic stress disorder (PTSD).\nMCQ 3.366"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[378],"source_qid":"3.364","duplicate_group_id":"exact-a7b73541ecec","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"1ab803cd4afa310f72b1","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":378,"source_qid":"3.364"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_multi_group","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"1ab803cd4afa310f72b1","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":378,"supporting_pages":[378],"source_qid":"3.364","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"; Australian Medical Council as : Hs\n| ESSCHOnS - MeniGnGONis ts 20, see i ee ee eee\nA. Truancy.\n/ B. A drop in grades at school.\nC. Angry outbursts.\nD. Arecent relationship break-up.\nE. Loss of employment. :\nMCQ 3.364\nRelatives report a gradual decline in memory and self-care skills in a 75-year-old man\nover several years. Examination reveals that he is disoriented in time, has poor short-\nterm memory, impaired planning, arithmetic and visuo spatial skills. There are no\n. other abnormal findings. Which one of the following is the most appropriate initial step\nin management?\nA. Lumbar puncture.\nB. Computed tomography (CT) of head.\nC. Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) of the b