thadone maintenance program, has been brought by friends to the Emergency\nDepartment after ‘collapsing’ at home within the past 30 minutes. He is usually on\n80mg methadone in daily take home dosage, but earlier that day had been given\nthree days supply as the clinic had to close for two days following a fire. His friends\nreport that he had vomited before lapsing into unconsciousness. On examination he is\ncomatose, centrally cyanosed and not responding to pain or command, his breathing\nis shallow with a respiratory rate of 8/min. His pulse rate is 56/min and thready and his\nBP is 70/SO0mmHg. After establishing an airway and 100% oxygenation, pharyngeal\nsuction and an intravenous line, which one of the following is the most important next\nstep in management?\n\n. Mannitol infusion.\nIntravenous clonidine.\n\n. Intravenous naloxone.\n\n. Sublingual buprenorphine.\nIntravenous naltrexone.\n\nMIO Cy"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["age"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"b9d64453fb69d69b808972747f1d157fbff4ef5d","duplicate_group_id":"exact-b9d64453fb69","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"d608018e8c5315c3c4ca","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":379,"source_qid":"3.367"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_expla