I An 80-year-old woman with a six-month history of depression has been admitted
f to hospital for a course of electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) after not responding to |
i combination selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors antidepressant/antipsychotic
therapy. She has had persisting low mood, weight loss of eight kilograms, suicidal
thoughts and concerns about her ‘rotting bowels’ for several months. She says she
is very anxious about commencing ECT the next morning and is now unable to get
to sleep. Her current medication is risperidone 1mg daily. Which one of the following
would be the most appropriate choice for overnight management of her insomnia?','{"A":"Diazepam.","B":"Lorazepam.","C":"Zopiclone.","D":"Additional risperidone.","E":"Amitriptyline.\nMCQ 3.371"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[380],"source_qid":"3.369","duplicate_group_id":"exact-967f73d18169","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"a45f368c8da30363b406","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":380,"source_qid":"3.369"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_multi_group","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"a45f368c8da30363b406","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":380,"supporting_pages":[380],"source_qid":"3.369","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"E. High density lipoprotein 1.2mmol/L (>1).\n: MCQ 3.370\nI An 80-year-old woman with a six-month history of depression has been admitted\nf to hospital for a course of electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) after not responding to |\ni combination selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors antidepressant/antipsychotic\ntherapy. She has had persisting low mood, weight loss of eight kilograms, suicidal\nthoughts and concerns about her ‘rotting bowels’ for several months. She says she\nis very anxious about commencing ECT the next morning and is now unable to get\nto sleep. Her current medication is risperidone 1mg daily. Which one of the following\nwould be the most appropriate choice for overnight management of her i