i change in her antipsychotic medication?','{"A":"Blood pressure 140/85mmHg.","B":"Glycosylated haemoglobin (HbA,_) level of 8% (<6).","C":"Body mass index (BMI) 24 (18-25).","D":"Thyroid-stimulating hormone 6.0mlU/L (0.3-5).","E":"High density lipoprotein 1.2mmol/L (>1).\n: MCQ 3.370"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[380],"source_qid":"3.369","duplicate_group_id":"exact-f022458e050a","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"f978286184ec86b20183","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":380,"source_qid":"3.369"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_multi_group","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"f978286184ec86b20183","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":380,"supporting_pages":[380],"source_qid":"3.369","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"MCQ 3.369\nA 25-year-old woman with schizophrenia, who has been treated with olanzapine in\nvariable dosage between 5-15mg daily for the past year, presents for the results of\nblood tests taken the week before. She has gained 15kg weight in the preceding nine\nmonths. She takes a high-calorie diet and has become more sedentary in the last four\nmonths since losing her job delivering pamphlets door-to-door. Both her father and\na younger sister are overweight. She takes the oral contraceptive pill and smokes 25\ncigarettes a day. Which one of the following would be the strongest indication for a\ni change in her a