a younger sister are overweight. She takes the oral contraceptive pill and smokes 25
cigarettes a day. Which one of the following would be the strongest indication for a
i change in her antipsychotic medication?','{"A":"Blood pressure 140/85mmHg.","B":"Glycosylated haemoglobin (HbA,_) level of 8% (<6).","C":"Body mass index (BMI) 24 (18-25).","D":"Thyroid-stimulating hormone 6.0mlU/L (0.3-5).","E":"High density lipoprotein 1.2mmol/L (>1).\n: MCQ 3.370\nI An 80-year-old woman with a six-month history of depression has been admitted\nf to hospital for a course of electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) after not responding to |\ni combination selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors antidepressant/antipsychotic\ntherapy. She has had persisting low mood, weight loss of eight kilograms, suicidal\nthoughts and concerns about her ‘rotting bowels’ for several months. She says she\nis very anxious about commencing ECT the next morning and is now unable to get\n\nto sleep. Her current medication is risperidone 1mg daily. Which one of the following\nwould be the most appropriate choice for overnight management of her insomnia?\nA. Diazepam.\n\nB. Lorazepam.\n\nC. Zopiclone.\nD. Additional risperidone.\nE. Amitriptyline.\nMCQ 3.371\nA 40-year-old high school teacher presents with increasing worry about intermittent\nleft lower abdominal pain, epigastric bloating and fluctuating constipation and\ndiarrhoea. Her symptoms began after a stressful parent-teacher meeting, during\nwhich she was confronted and abused by an irate parent, about three months ago.\nShe has had similar episodes in the past since her adolescence and reports that\nalthough the pain is relieved by defaecation, she is afraid that she may have bowel |\n| cancer. On examination she is tender in her left iliac fossa over her sigmoid colon.\nThere is no family history of bowel disease, no weight loss, fever or rectal bleeding. :\nWhich one of the following is most likely to improve her overall symptoms and general |\nwell-being?\nA. Aloe vera.\nH B. Acupuncture. ;\n| C. High fibre diet.\n} D. Amitriptyline.\n| E. Fluoxetine.\n\n362 ;"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.369","duplicate_group_id":"exact-d197e6f316a5","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"fa8f60018f78177e6451","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":380,"source_qid":"3.369"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"fa8f60018f78177e6451","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":380,"source_qid":"3.369","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council > free eee\n| Section 3- Menta ne SL A, tae (ein ry el ES a pWighas Enea ar eee.\nMCQ 3.369\nA 25-year-old woman with schizophrenia, who has been treated with olanzapine in\nvariable dosage between 5-15mg daily for the past year, presents for the results of\nblood tests taken the week before. She has gained 15kg weight in the preceding nine\nmonths. She takes a high-calorie diet and has become more sedentary in the last four\nmonths since losing her job delivering pamphlets door-to-door. Both her father and\na younger sister are overweight. She takes the oral contraceptive pill and smokes 25\ncigarettes a day. Which one of the following would be the strongest indication for a\ni change in her antipsychotic medication?","options":{"A":"Blood pressure 140/85mmHg.","B":"Glycosylated haemoglobin (HbA,_) level of 8% (<6).","C":"Body mass index (BMI) 24 (18-25).","D":"Thyroid-stimulating hormone 6.0mlU/L (0.3-5).","E":"High density lipoprotein 1.2mmol/L (>1).\n: MCQ 3.370\nI An 80-year-old woman with a six-month history of depression has been admitted\nf to hospital for a course of electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) after not responding to |\ni combination selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors antidepressant/antipsychotic\ntherapy. She has had persisting low mood, weight loss of eight kilograms, suicidal\nthoughts and concerns about her ‘rotting bowels’ for several months. She says she\nis very anxious about commencing ECT the next morning and is now unable to get\n\nto sleep. Her current medication is risperidone 1mg daily. Which one of the following\nwould be the most appropriate choice for overnight management of her insomnia?\nA. Diazepam.\n\nB. Lorazepam.\n\nC. Zopiclone.\nD. Additional risperidone.\nE. Amitriptyline.\nMCQ 3.371\nA 40-year-old high school teacher presents with increasing worry about intermittent\nleft lower abdominal pain, epigastric bloating and fluctuating constipation and\ndiarrhoea. Her symptoms began after a stressful parent-teacher meeting, during\nwhich she was confronted and abused by an irate parent, about three months ago.\nShe has had similar episodes in the past since her adolescence and reports that\nalthough the pain is relieved by defaecation, she is afraid that she may have bowel |\n| cancer. On examination she is tender in her left iliac fossa over her sigmoid colon.\nThere is no family history of bowel disease, no weight loss, fever or rectal bleeding. :\nWhich one of the following is most likely to improve her overall symptoms and general |\nwell-being?\nA. Aloe vera.\nH B. Acupuncture. ;\n| C. High fibre diet.\n} D. Amitriptyline.\n| E. Fluoxetine.\n\n362 ;"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["age","contracept"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_pars