Section 3- Mental Health','{"A":"Diazepam syrup.","B":"Intramuscular diazepam.","C":"Intravenous diazepam.","D":"Intramuscular midazolam.","E":"Intramuscular droperidol.\n\nMCQ 3.375\n\nA 65-year-old woman is admitted to hospital with sudden onset of agitation, confusion\nand fever for the past 12 months. She has been taking sertraline for depression. She\nhas also been taking some over-the-counter medications for the last week. Her BP\nis 180/80mmHg, temperature 37.8°C, pulse 110/min and regular. She has a coarse\ntremor of both hands, muscle tone is normal but reflexes are generally increased. The\noptic fundi show grade Il hypertensive changes. Her full blood count, chest X-ray,\nurine examination and serum creatine kinase (CK) are all normal. Which one of the\nfollowing is the most likely diagnosis?\n\nA. Neuroleptic malignant syndrome.\nB. Serotonin syndrome.\n\nC. Herpes encephalitis.\n\nD. Systemic sepsis.\n\nE. Hypertensive encephalopathy.\n\nMCQ 3.376\n\nAn 80-year-old woman presents with a history of recurrent falls. She lives at home\nalone. She has hypertension treated with perindopril 5mg daily. Over the past six\nweeks she has developed cognitive impairment for which she receives haloperidol\nImg nocte to manage nocturnal wandering. Her Mini-Mental State Examination\n(MMSE) score is 24/30. Her BP and pulse readings are BP 154/6é6mmHg, pulse 80/\nmin regular (supine), BP 136/60mmHg, 84/min (standing). She has some involuntary\nmovements of her face and tongue, a slow small-paced gait, and increased muscle\ntone in all limbs. Which one of the following is the most appropriate next step in\nmanagement?\n\n. Commence levodopa.\nCommence benztropine mesylate.\n. Commence selegiline.\n. Cease perindopril.\nCease haloperidol.\n\nMOQ F >\n\nMCQ 3.377\n\nRelatives report a gradual decline in memory and self-care skills in a 70-year-old\nwoman over several years. Examination shows that she is disoriented in time, has poor\nshort-term memory, impaired planning, arithmetic and visuospatial skills. There are no\n\nother abnormal clinical or imaging findings. Which one of the following is the most\nlikely diagnosis?"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.375","duplicate_group_id":"exact-d88cfb65a34a","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"ec6e041df61b1a26964c","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":382,"source_qid":"3.375"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"ec6e041df61b1a26964c","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":382,"source_qid":"3.375","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council\nSection 3- Mental Health","options":{"A":"Diazepam syrup.","B":"Intramuscular diazepam.","C":"Intravenous diazepam.","D":"Intramuscular midazolam.","E":"Intramuscular droperidol.\n\nMCQ 3.375\n\nA 65-year-old woman is admitted to hospital with sudden onset of agitation, confusion\nand fever for the past 12 months. She has been taking sertraline for depression. She\nhas also been taking some over-the-counter medications for the last week. Her BP\nis 180/80mmHg, temperature 37.8°C, pulse 110/min and regular. She has a coarse\ntremor of both hands, muscle tone is normal but reflexes are generally increased. The\noptic fundi show grade Il hypertensive changes. Her full blood count, chest X-ray,\nurine examination and serum creatine kinase (CK) are all normal. Which one of the\nfollowing is the most