MCQ 3.380
A local community group asks you to give a brief presentation to its members on
weight loss and obesity issues, and discuss the meaning of ‘body mass index’ (BMI).
Which one of the following concepts about BMI would be the most appropriate to
include?','{"A":"Combined with waist circumference BMI is the most useful indicator of health risk.","B":"Weight/standard weight ratio is less reliable than BMI when assessing obesity in\nchildren.","C":"Adjust upper limit of normal for BMI upwards for people from South-East Asia.","D":". Bioimpedence analysis is a more useful measure of obesity than BMI in body\nbuilders.","E":"BMI can overestimate body fat in the elderly.\n\nsecre oesesasesnapentsetesetesnannesos2S0ciSStSStt tt SaSSSSeS SSS SLT\n\nMCQ 3.381\n\nWhich one of the following life events is the most significant sociodemographic\npredictor of stress-related physical illness?\n\nA. Unemployment.\nB. Imprisonment.\nC. Illness of children.\nD. Marital disruption.\nE. Bankruptcy.\n\n soenensoerestansssnsesnsseeesunsssssnesheessattsitssoteets SS SftsStSssS Sts SSSesSSsSSneetSSsstssSSStsSSSSveeNSSSSSsestSSSSosSSSnsSSsSSsiScSneS\n\nMCQ 3.382\n\nA 45-year-old man presents with shortness of breath on exertion and some weight\nloss. He is a non-smoker and has worked for 15 years in an electricity-generating plant\nin a regional town. He is married with two children and is worried about the effect\nof his breathlessness on his capacity to earn a living for his family. Which one of the\nfollowing is the most likely contributing factor to his condition?\n\nPassive smoking at work.\nAsbestos exposure.\n\n. Environmental coal dust.\n\nAir pollution.\n\nWood smoke from home heater.\n\nMOOR >"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.379","duplicate_group_id":"exact-ee22eab48a49","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"33eba6a89fe704d32758","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":385,"source_qid":"3.379"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-202