MCQ 3.388
A 32-year-old Indigenous woman attends a general practice with an upper respiratory
tract infection. You advise her about symptom management and that no other
treatment is needed at this time. Which one of the following is likely to be the most
relevant opportunistic screening assessment to do at this consultation?
Alcohol consumption.
Visual acuity.
. Microalbuminuria.
Mammogram.
Papanicolaou (Pap) smear.
MOQ >
MCQ 3.389
Which one of the following interventions is an example of primary prevention?
Tetanus prophylaxis.
Screening sigmoidoscopy.
. Performance of a Papanicolaou (Pap) smear.
BP screening.
Mantoux skin test for tuberculosis.
MOQRP>
MCQ 3.390
A 39-year-old woman presents for her Papanicolaou (Pap) smear two years after her
previous normal Pap smear result. She has not had sexual relationships for over two
years and is well. She asks if she should have a check for sexually transmitted diseases
while she is having her Pap smear. Which one of the following is the most appropriate
reason for advising against testing for chlamydia?','{"A":"The test for chlamydia is unreliable.","B":"She would have had symptoms by now if infection was present.","C":"Chlamydia is uncommon in her age group.","D":"First catch urine polymerase chain reaction (PCR) is more sensitive.","E":"She has had no recent sexual partners.\n\nMCQ 3.391\n\nA 45-year-old woman presents with a two-day history of abdominal cramping and\nbloody diarrhoea. On further questioning, she tells you that she had been on a\ntwo-week vacation touring Central America. She occasionally ate some of the local\nfoods, especially fresh fruits and salad, but was careful about her drinking water. She\nhas felt well for the past month since returning from the trip until the current symptoms\nstarted two days ago. She has no other history of travel or exposure to infectious agents.\nWhich one of the following organisms is most likely to be causing her symptoms?"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.388","duplicate_group_id":"exact-5d749e35c2d9","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"6ef224ccf6e106f1f5c5","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":387,"source_qid":"3.388"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"6ef224ccf6e106f1f5c5","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":387,"source_qid":"3.388","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council\n. Alow incidence of the congenital condition in the community.\nThe congenital condition has limited impact on life expectancy.\n. Early treatment provides a better quality of life than with late diagnosis.\n. There is a moderately high level of risk with the screening procedure.\nThe screening procedure is low cost.\nGaie) @y.2) 23\nMCQ 3.388\nA 32-year-old Indigenous woman attends a general practice with an upper respiratory\ntract infection. You advise her about symptom management and that no other\ntreatment is needed at this time. Which one of the following is likely to be the most\nrelevant opportunistic screening assessment to do at this consultation?\nAlcohol consumption.\nVisual acuity.\n. Microalbuminuria.\nMammogram.\nPapanicolaou (Pap) smear.\nMOQ >\nMCQ 3.389\nWhich one of the following interventions is an example of primary prevention?\nTetanus prophylaxis.\nScreening sigmoidoscopy.\n. Performance of a Papanicolaou (Pap) smear.\nBP screening.\nMantoux skin test for tuberculosis.\nMOQRP>\nMCQ 3.390\nA 39-year-old woman presents for her Papanicolaou (Pap) smear two years after her\nprevious normal Pap smear result. She has not had sexual relationships for over two\nyears and is well. She asks if she should have a check for sexually transmitted diseases\nwhile she is having her Pap smear. Which one of the following is the most appropriate\nreason for advising against testing for chlamydia?","options":{"A":"The test for chlamydia is unreliable.","B":"She would have had symptoms by now if infection was present.","C":"Chlamydia is uncommon in her age group.","D":"First catch urine polymerase chain reaction (PCR) is more sensitive.","E":"She has had no recent sexual partners.\n\nMCQ 3.391\n\nA 45-year-old woman presents with a two-day history of abdominal cramping and\nbloody diarrhoea. On further questioning, she tells you that she had been on a\ntwo-week vacation touring Central America. She occasionally ate some of the local\nfoods, especially fresh fruits and salad, but was careful about her drinking water. She\nhas felt well for the past month since returning from the trip until the current symptoms\nstarted two days ago. She has no other history of travel or exposure to infectious agents.\nWhich one of the following organisms is most likely to be causing her symptoms?"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","management","prophyl","screen","screening","treatment"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"5d749e35c2d9e3ce6d4ae80449878e676ec035ad","duplicate_group_id":"exact-5d749e35c2d9","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"6ef224ccf6e106f1f5c5","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":387,"source_qid":"3.388"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk,record_json=excluded.record_json,active_quiz=excluded.active_quiz,import_version=excluded.import_version,imported_at=excluded.imported_at;
