urine microscopy, urea, electrolytes, and liver function tests. Apart from a slightly
low platelet count (105x10%/L) and mildly raised liver enzymes (<1.5 normal) the
remaining test results were normal. He is not sure about his vaccination status. He had
taken doxycycline most of the days while away, and stopped this a week ago. On
| examination, he looks unwell, has a temperature of 38°C, the throat is congested and
he has vague epigastric tenderness. Which one of the following conditions is the most
at important to exclude by a further diagnostic test?','{"A":"Plasmodium falciparum malaria.","B":"Plasmodium vivax malaria.","C":"Hepatitis A.","D":"Infectious mononucleosis.","E":"Enteric fever.\nMCQ 3.398"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[389],"source_qid":"3.396","duplicate_group_id":"exact-55c3293c618f","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"c269a4a3689d201a11fa","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":389,"source_qid":"3.396"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_multi_group","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"c269a4a3689d201a11fa","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":389,"supporting_pages":[389],"source_qid":"3.396","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"He was seen by the after-hours doctor who had organised a full blood count,\nurine microscopy, urea, electrolytes, and liver function tests. Apart from a slightly\nlow platelet count (105x10%/L) and mildly raised liver enzymes (<1.5 normal) the\nremaining test results were normal. He is not sure about his vaccination status. He had\ntaken doxycycline most of the days while away, and stopped this a week ago. On\n| examination, he looks unwell, has a temperature of 38°C, the throat is congested and\nhe has vague epigastric tenderness. Which one of the following conditions is the most\nat important to exclude by a further diagnostic test?","options":{"A":"Plasmodium falciparum malaria.","B":"P