Section 3 — Population, Community Health and Ethics
eee
MCQ 3.406
A 10-year-old boy presents with urinary frequency. He has
a past history of recurrent urinary tract infections. Physical
examination is normal. A midstream urine specimen shows
protein+ and a trace of blood with no organisms seen
or grown on culture. A plain abdominal X-ray is normal
and renal ultrasound shows a dilated renal pelvis on the
right. A micturating cystourethrogram is performed and
is illustrated. Which one of the following is the most likely
diagnosis?
Vesicoureteric reflux.
Bladder neck obstruction.
Pelviureteric junction obstruction.
Neurogenic bladder.
Congenital hydronephrosis.
—__—_———————
MCQ 3.407
MOOS>
A 20-year-old man requests a vasectomy. He has been in a stable heterosexual
relationship for three years with the same partner and they feel strongly that they do
not want children now or in the future. His partner does not wish to continue taking the
contraceptive pill, and he does not wish to use condoms. Which one of the following
responses is most appropriate to his request?','{"A":"You would not sanction the operation until he is over 21.","B":"You would not sanction the operation under the circumstances because of its\nirreversibility.","C":"You wish to talk to his partner to obtain her consent.","D":"You will go ahead to make the arrangements.","E":"You would advise him fully of the Pros and cons of the procedure.\n\nOO eee\n\nMCQ 3.408\n\nWhich one of the following potential risk factors results in the highest risk for ischaemic\nstroke?\n\nHypercholesterolaemia.\n\nObesity.\n\n. Smoking.\n\n. Non-insulin-dependent (Type 2) diabetes.\nHypertension.\n\nMOQ2>"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.406","duplicate_group_id":"exact-c9494e0da9b6","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"16934ae25107ff3760da","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":392,"source_qid":"3.406"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"16934ae25107ff3760da","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":392,"source_qid":"3.406","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council\nSection 3 — Population, Community Health and Ethics\neee\nMCQ 3.406\nA 10-year-old boy presents with urinary frequency. He has\na past history of recurrent urinary tract infections. Physical\nexamination is normal. A midstream urine specimen shows\nprotein+ and a trace of blood with no organisms seen\nor grown on culture. A plain abdominal X-ray is normal\nand renal ultrasound shows a dilated renal pelvis on the\nright. A micturating cystourethrogram is performed and\nis illustrated. Which one of the following is the most likely\ndiagnosis?\nVesicoureteric reflux.\nBladder neck obstruction.\nPelviureteric junction obstruction.\nNeurogenic bladder.\nCongenital hydronephrosis.\n—__—_———————\nMCQ 3.407\nMOOS>\nA 20-year-old man requests a vasectomy. He has been in a stable heterosexual\nrelationship for three years with the same partner and they feel strongly that they do\nnot want children now or in the future. His partner does not wish to continue taking the\ncontraceptive pill, and he does not wish to use condoms. Which one of the following\nresponses is most appropriate to his request?","options":{"A":"You would not sanction the operation until he is over 21.","B":"You would not sanction the operation under the circumstances because of its\nirreversibility.","C":"You wish to talk to his partner to obtain her consent.","D":"You will go ahead to make the arrangements.","E":"You would advise him fully of the Pros and cons of the procedure.\n\nOO eee\n\nMCQ 3.408\n\nWhich one of the following potential risk factors results in the highest risk for ischaemic\nstroke?\n\nHypercholesterolaemia.\n\nObesity.\n\n. Smoking.\n\n. Non-insulin-dependent (Type 2) diabetes.\nHypertension.\n\nMOQ2>"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["contracept"],"likely_visual_question":true,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"c9494e0da9b66b51151c906dce6b0a1a9d387ac5","duplicate_group_id":"exact-c9494e0da9b6","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"16934ae25107ff3760da","record_type":"