MCQ 3.097
The clinical picture fits best the progressive s fn
obstructive stricturing of lower oesophagus
by a cicatrising peptic oesophageal
stricture secondary to reflux oesophagitis.
Treatment of reflux oesophagitis symptoms
with simple antacids/alkalis may give {
symptomatic relief, but these agents
do not influence the natural history. The ¥
painful dysphagia of acid reflux will lessen : |
as the stricture progresses, reflux diminishes | }
and obstructive symptoms predominate.
}
Each of the other conditions can be 5 5 |
associated with progressive dysphagia, Peptic oesophageal stricture above a |
but the pattern fits a peptic oesophageal sliding hiatus hernia
