case of congestive heart failure. He had been
Stable on enalapril, metoprolol and digoxin
until three weeks ago when his wife passed
away from breast cancer. Since then, he
stopped taking his medication. Today, he is
brought to the emergency department by his
son, with complaints of shortness of breath,
night coughs and ankle edema. On
examination, he has a blood pressure of
90/75mmdHg, heart rate of 68 bpm, and
respiratory rate of 26 breaths per minute. On
auscultation, an S3 gallop is noted, but there
is no crackle. You decide to start him on
medication again. Which one of the following
would be the best option to start with?','{"A":"Start him on enalapril.","B":"Start him on metoprolol.","C":"Start him on digoxin.","D":"Start him on enalapril, digoxin and\nmetoprolol at the same time.","E":"Start him on enalapril and\nmetoprolol."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 CVS (1).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-9ffaa4d9ec29","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"58ad4d20313157b715b5","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 CVS (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 CVS (1).pdf","source_page":139,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"58ad4d20313157b715b5","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 CVS (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 CVS (1).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":139,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Cardiology","stem":"Steven is a 65-year-old man, who is a known\ncase of congestive heart failure. He had been\nStable on enalapril, metoprolol and digoxin\nuntil three weeks ago when his wife passed\naway from breast cancer. Since then, he\nstopped taking his medication. Today, he is\nbrought to the emergency department by his\nson, with complaints of shortness of breath,\nnight coughs and ankle edema. On\nexamination, he has a blood pressure of\n90/75mmdHg, heart rate of 68 bpm, and\nrespiratory rate of 26 breaths per minute. On\nauscultation, an S3 gallop is noted, but there\nis no crackle. You decide to start him on\nmedication again. Which one of the following\nwould be the best option to start with?","options":{"A":"Start him on enalapril.","B":"Start him on metoprolol.","C":"Start him on digoxin.","D":"Start him on enalapril, digoxin and\nmetoprolol at the same time.","E":"Start him on enalapril 