department with sudden onset right-sided leg
pain and paresthesia. On physical
examination, the distal pulses of the right leg
are absent and the limb is cold. A CT
angiography is arranged showing thrombotic
occlusion of the right femoral artery. Which
one of the following is the next best step in
management?','{"A":"Intravenous infusion of heparin\nand emergency embolectomy.","B":"Intravenous infusion of heparin for\n24 hours and review.","C":"Complete bed rest with a\ncompression bandage and leg\nelevation.","D":"Hp Start the patient on warfarin.","E":"Start the patient on aspirin and\nclopidogrel."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 CVS (1).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-ad17fc3535a3","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"7b877b324257e616790e","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 CVS (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 CVS (1).pdf","source_page":145,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"ed0d008536fcd882c786","record_type":"visual_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 CVS (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 CVS (1).pdf","source_page":144,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"a8449d16ef6ff39fa687","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":54,"source_qid":"264"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"7b877b324257e616790e","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 CVS (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 CVS (1).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":145,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Cardiology","stem":"A 65-year-old man presents to the emergency\ndepartment with sudden onset right-sided leg\npain and paresthesia. On physical\nexamination, the distal pulses of the right leg\nare absent and the limb is cold. A CT\nangiography is arranged showing thrombotic\nocclusion of the right femoral artery. Which\none of the following is the next best step in\nmanagement?","options":{"A":"Intravenous infusion